      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-07T23:08:53Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(app): judge a boring bar's head and shank on its cutting feeds\n\nThe rapid law (#103) judged the bar's whole body on its rapids and the\nenvelope verdict judged the nose's cut, so the head and shank rode\nevery plunge, lead and pass unjudged against the stock. The new\nturning_feeds law samples each feed of a Bore tool along its length.\nAt each instant it reads the bar's head (flute_len up the axis) and\nshank (shank_len above it), at the spans turning::bar_spans gives,\nagainst the revolved part, and against the stock less the drills\nahead, the turning ops ahead, the program ahead's faced end, this\npath's earlier feeds and this feed's own kerf up to that instant. The\nnose's own cut is never judged here. A body in the part or in stock\nstill standing is a ShankHit on that move, which blocks the post (one\nper move; a move the solid law already named is not named twice).\n\nThe Meridian context in generate is built once and shared by the rapid\nand feed laws; turning_rapids' meridian helpers become pub(super).\n\nPins (turning_bore):\n- a_bar_whose_head_rides_the_uncut_band_above_its_nose_is_convicted\n  (Ø10 bar, Ø12 bore over a Ø10.6 pilot: the head's edge rides the\n  uncut band above the nose; fails on main, which posts it clean)\n- a_stepped_bar_whose_shank_rubs_the_wall_during_the_ride_is_convicted\n  (head Ø8, shank Ø12, Ø14 bore: ShankHit on the part on the ride)\n- a_bored_op_runs_clean_in_the_document stays clean.\n\nFixes #146\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
