      "message": "fix(app): credit a bore op ahead with its whole nose kerf\n\nReview B1 on PR #185: rest::ahead filled `Ahead.nose` for Turning tools\nonly, so a Bore op ahead was credited along its nose-centre line. The\nfeed body law then refused a normal rough-then-finish bore (a 0.8 nose\nbar, then a 0.4 one, over a Ø10.9 pilot into the Ø12 hole). Bore now\nstates its nose too. The prior plan refuses every turning op ahead but\nnose-cut Facing, so it never sweeps a bore's nose. A dependent of a bore\nop hashes the nose byte into its stamp and reads Stale once.\n\nAlso from the review:\n- N1: a feed's own trail credits only a straight or spindle-turn kerf.\n- N2: a bar piece longer than the sample cap is read at a coarser pitch,\n  never cut short.\n- N3: the credits are asked once per material point.\n\nThe #146 pins move to tests/turning_bore_feeds.rs (turning_bore.rs\nstood at the 400-line law), plus\na_finishing_bar_riding_where_a_rougher_bar_cut_is_clean, which fails\nwithout the ahead fix.\n\nRefs #146\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
